2. Heap (Dynamic & Runtime)
When: Memory is allocated on the heap at runtime using specific commands (e.g., malloc in C, new in C++ or Java).
What: It stores data that needs to persist beyond the function that created it, or data whose size is not known until the program is running.
Key Traits: Slower than stack, large size, requires manual management (in C/C++) or garbage collection (in Java/Python). 
